  "summary": "Preserve historical Shop evidence, restore exact current regeneration, and execute the readable public walkthrough.",
  "why": "Luis approved the Pareto evidence repair and readable Shop demonstration. The three baseline failures trace to e4fa5fd changing a compiler diagnostic and its attested producer fingerprint; all three pass at the direct parent ca0d121. Existing graphs and Shop answers are unchanged. Eight historical files remain byte-identical, a separate current generation restores exact comparisons, and the default evidence output now uses build rather than historical fixtures. A verbatim public query is exercised against the real from-empty five-plan run; a declared capture gap is recovered after admission and reopen. Evidence RED 7 failed and 8 passed, GREEN 15 passed; walkthrough RED 1 failed and 1 passed; documented-path plus docs controls 27 passed; complete compiler Pareto and Shop gate 731 passed with no failures or skips. No Core runtime, ontology, source, mapping, package, paper, stable-wire or release change. Re-entry immutable-context composition remains a separate unimplemented requirement.",
